   "l": "The next:\nthey hold him in contempt.",
   "v": true,
   "n": "Four rungs down, and every one of them is measured in what the people do, never in what the ruler does. The best ruler is described only by the bare fact that the people know he exists; the worst, only by their contempt. Nothing is said about policy at all — which is the argument. Note that being loved and praised is already the second rung, not the first."
